<!--
    Weight model v2 of cattle (scripts/animal/RLGrowth.lua): each physical breed's female and male
    reference growth curve and mean birth weight, the breed names maps use for them, the animal
    types bound to a breed's curve as a stand-in, and the model's settings. Source: the all-cattle
    weight design v2 (FS25_CowBreeds_离线准备_2026-10-07/all-cattle-weight-design-v2.md and its
    all-cattle-weight-profiles-v2.json). Every number here is a design candidate, not a measured
    breed value; the status of each profile says where it stands.

    The console command rlWeightProfiles lists every cattle subtype the game has loaded (base,
    Cow Breeds pack, map), the profile it resolves to, its curve, and which of its old weight
    settings come from a config file.

    enabled        On: covered cattle grow on these curves (with the body condition feature on,
                   bodyCondition.xml). Off: every animal keeps the old weight rules; states saved
                   by the model are kept for when it is switched on again.

    Curves
    profile name   A breed name as subtypes carry it (animals.xml breed="...").
            status BASE_XML_UNREVALIDATED  this mod's breeds: adult = animals.xml targetWeight
                   PACK_REVIEW_ONLY        Cow Breeds pack: research candidates (the pack's own
                                           targetWeight is not used for growth), with the seven
                                           beef breeds' confirmed admission weights as knots
                   MAP_REVIEW_ONLY         breeds only a map brings: research candidates
            birthFemaleKg  Mean birth weight of a single heifer calf from an average dam; a bull
                   calf is maleBirthFactor heavier (or the profile's own maleBirthFactor).
    female / male knots  month:kg after birth, the last one the adult plateau. Between knots the
                   curve is a monotone cubic Hermite (no overshoot, weight and gain continuous);
                   after the last it is flat. Each animal grows on this curve x its size gene,
                   from its actual birth weight (the difference to the mean fades out by
                   birthFadeMonths).
    alias breed    A breed name a map uses for a profile's breed: its subtypes grow on that
            profile profile's curve and keep their own name and identity.
    typeBinding    An animal type outside COW put on a profile's curve as a stand-in, where the
                   game holds its animals as individuals: Hof Bergmann's MILKCOW (its subtype has
                   no weights and does not reproduce) on the Holstein female curve. Its milk and
                   price keep their own rules; enabled="false" leaves the type out. Where the type
                   exists only as vanilla clusters the binding does nothing (the report says so).

    A breed that is neither a profile nor an alias is reported UNRESOLVED and keeps the old rules:
    it never falls into another breed's curve silently.

    Settings (root)
    maleBirthFactor   Bull calf / heifer calf birth weight.
    birthWeightCV     Spread of birth weights (coefficient of variation), drawn normal around
    birthTruncateSD   the birth's mean and drawn again beyond this many standard deviations.
    birthGeneEffect   Birth weight x (1 + this x (metabolism - 1)).
    firstBirthFactor  A heifer's first calf.
    litter2/3/4       Each calf of twins, triplets, four or more.
    damReserveEffect  The dam's body reserve r: x (1 + this x (r - referenceReserve)), between
    damFactorMin/Max  these. A dam with no reserve on record counts as 1.
    geneSpan          z = (metabolism - 1) / geneSpan, clamped to -1..1.
    sizeGeneEffect    Adult weight x (1 + this x z).
    speedGeneEffect   Development speed x (1 + this x z).
    maintenanceGeneEffect  Maintenance and the feed it asks for x (1 + this x z).
    birthFadeMonths   The animal's own birth weight fades into the reference curve by this age.
    castratedSpeed    A steer develops at this speed of a bull's (no step: the change takes
    transitionMonths  about this long, as does a change of intake capacity at calving or drying).
    underweightRatio  Below this share of its curve at its age an animal loses health.
    frameFloorRatio   Numerical floor: the frame is never broken down below this share of the
                      frame at birth. It is no part of the birth calibration.

    To change these without editing the mod, copy this file to
    modSettings/FS25_RealisticLivestockRM/weightProfiles.xml; that copy then replaces this file
    entirely. An invalid file switches the model off and logs why.
-->
<weightProfiles enabled="true"
    maleBirthFactor="1.07" birthWeightCV="0.10" birthTruncateSD="2.5" birthGeneEffect="0.05"
    firstBirthFactor="0.93" litter2="0.85" litter3="0.75" litter4="0.70"
    damReserveEffect="0.25" damFactorMin="0.90" damFactorMax="1.03"
    geneSpan="0.75" sizeGeneEffect="0.12" speedGeneEffect="0.10" maintenanceGeneEffect="0.15"
    birthFadeMonths="6" castratedSpeed="0.90" transitionMonths="0.5" underweightRatio="0.70"
    frameFloorRatio="0.5">

